The link above is already a no-key-item-wish deathless ascnesion in 1 
turn. Unless you consider the automatic acquisition of the amulet 
cheating (any more than you are already 'cheating').

> You can ascend no-key-item-wish-deathless in under 20 turns: levelport
> to the sanctum level (wizmode level teleport allows entrance without
> doing the invocation), teleport into the temple, wish for a wand of
> death, shoot the high priest/ess, pick up the amulet, levelport to the
> Astral Plane, 

I think it's a bit strange to consider 'cheaty' levelporting to the 
sanctum less cheaty than cheaty levelporting to the Planes, as per the 
original 1-turn method provided in the link. Where do you draw the line? 
Clearly not at no-key-item-wish-deathless, because then it's just that 1 
turn needed.

> teleport to your altar (might need to check out more
> than one altar), ascend; i'm assuming that wishing for a co-aligned
> altar on your arrival spot also counts as wishing for a key item.

OK, then it would be a 2-4 turn thing unless you have some trouble with 
the intra-level teleportation / altar locating.

[...]
> If you want to do the invocation properly, the debug mode monster
> generation offers a shortcut to get hold of the invocation items -
> quest nemeses and Vlad are always generated carrying the respective
> unique items. Wizmode allows you to generate _any_ nemesis, even tame.
> Only Rodney doesn't start out carrying the book, you have to loot his
> original abode (but you can nuke him via genociding '*' without losing
> the book).

Neat trick with generating! And doing the invocation properly makes 
things a bit interesting again, almost getting to the level where there 
might be some different strategies. 
I tried to come up with some interesting rules in the post
news:<MPG.200d62dcbb0f693f98984a@130.133.1.4> but perhaps ruling out 
CTRL+G should also be needed, or just rule out CTRL+G for uniques and 
perhaps something against genocides too. Neh, now we're soon getting 
back to normal nonwizmode, perhaps that why it is the standard mode 
really, it's the most interesting way to play the game. :)

